title: Famine on the Volga
subtitle: Russia is starving, and Münzenberg asks the party for money.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 3
max-visits: 1

= Famine on the Volga

The famine on the Volga has killed hundreds of thousands since the summer. Willi Münzenberg's Workers' International Relief collects flour, money and tools in every German city, and its posters of starving children hang in union halls that would never hang ours. Münzenberg wants the party's treasury behind it. The district treasurers say the party cannot pay its own printers.

- @give: Give him what we have.
- @keep: Collect in the works, and keep the treasury for the party.

@give
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Lenin is grateful, and Münzenberg builds something that will outlast the famine.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing in the treasury to give.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e22_famine = 1;
RG.ecci('lenin', 8);
Q.worker_support += 3;
!}

Ships leave Hamburg with flour and machine parts. Münzenberg keeps the lists of every helper and every kitchen, and tells the Zentrale it can borrow them whenever it is hungry itself.

@keep
subtitle: The cells collect where they can.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_famine = 2;
Q.worker_support += 1;
!}

The tins go round the works. Münzenberg tells Moscow the Germans are mean.
